=== THE RELATIONAL READING: triangular = the relation itself ===
  T_n (triangular): [0, 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, 28, 36]
  T_{n-1} = C(n,2) = |E(K_n)| = # arcs of a tournament on n vertices:
    [(2, 1), (3, 3), (4, 6), (5, 10), (6, 15), (7, 21), (8, 28)]
  staircase delta_{n-2} tile count = C(n-1,2) = T_{n-2}  (the tiling triangle IS triangular-sized):
    [(3, 1), (4, 3), (5, 6), (6, 10), (7, 15), (8, 21)]
  2^{C(n,2)} = 2^triangular = # LABELED GRAPHS on n vertices:
    [1, 2, 8, 64, 1024, 32768] (= 1,2,8,64,1024,32768)
  2^{C(n-1,2)} = # TILINGS (fixed base path) = the tournament tiling hypercube Q_{T_{n-2}}:
    [1, 2, 8, 64, 1024, 32768]
  => x = triangular number is the NATURAL graph/tournament value of the n*2^x+1 exponent:
     n=1, x=T_m gives 2^{T_m}+1 = (#tilings)+1 = the observer-augmented tiling count.
     2^T_1+1 = 2^1+1 = 3
     2^T_2+1 = 2^3+1 = 9
     2^T_3+1 = 2^6+1 = 65
     2^T_4+1 = 2^10+1 = 1025
     2^T_5+1 = 2^15+1 = 32769

